From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 221] panvk: carry deferred fragment waits across primary command buffers
Generated-by: LLM

At the end of a primary command buffer every deferred wait of the
vertex/tiler and compute subqueues on the fragment subqueue (patches
204, 208, 209) was emitted.  DXVK ends a primary every few render
passes, so in Assassin's Creed (D3D9) the next one's geometry always
waited for all fragment work so far: 132 waits/s, geometry and fragment
work overlapping 1% of the time.  The end of a primary now stores the
fragment point of a pending deferred wait in the subqueue context, and
each primary starts with a deferred wait on that point, emitted
(conditionally on the GPU) under the same rules as any deferred wait.
Nothing waits more than before, only later, and a carried-in wait is
emitted at the end of the next command buffer at the latest, so the
subqueue runs at most one command buffer ahead of fragment work
(unbounded run-ahead corrupted Assassin's Creed's menu with 220).  PANVK_LAZY_CROSS=0
restores the old behaviour.  A biblioklept who returns the books on
the next visit.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/220

